<para><emphasis>Using Standard Form and Intercepts to Graph</emphasis></para>
<para> Standard form, \(Ax + By = C\), is helpful for finding the \(x\)-intercepts and \(y\)-intercepts of an equation. </para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="943d7507-2a41-427c-b862-a04006a2eb93" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q#6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d693b658-f7c3-4288-9f1b-0baf9a491166" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="0">
    <problem>
      <para> For questions 6 - 11, </para>
      <blockquote>Use the equation \(6x -4y=24\).</blockquote>
      <para>What is the value of \(y\) at the \(x\)-intercept?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 0</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="8bab532e-ecf3-48f9-a6e5-4505f13ce64e" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="4">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the \(x\)-intercept of the equation?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 4</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#8-->
  <exercise data-content-id="04605dc6-d8fc-45b1-a167-4208032018fe" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="4">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the value of \(x\) at the \(y\)-intercept?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 0</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#9-->
  <exercise data-content-id="59849d8c-16fa-497f-85ed-a7fc1d68615a" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="4">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the \(y\)-intercept of the equation?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! -6</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
